%I A400564 #11 Sep 30 2026 08:54:24
%S A400564 2,3,2,4,4,5,5,7,5,9,7,10,8,13,8,15,10,17,11,20,11,23,13,25,14,29,14,
%T A400564 32,16,35,17,39,17,43,19,46,20,51,20,55,22,59,23,64,23,69,25,73,26,79,
%U A400564 26,84,28,89,29,95,29,101,31,106,32,113,32,119,34,125,35,132
%N A400564 Number of S_3 orbits of nonnegative integer vectors (x, y, z) != (0,0,0) having coordinate sum equal to n.
%C A400564 Counts the orbits under the action of the symmetric group S_3 on non-zero triples (x, y, z) in Z_{>=0}^3 such that the sum of the first coordinate across all permutations in the orbit equals n.
%C A400564 These numbers serve as the multiset generator exponents in the generating function for S_3-symmetric 3D vector partitions of (n, n, n) (A400544).
%C A400564 Equivalently, a(n) decomposes into three geometric orbit types:
%C A400564 - Orbits of size 1 (diagonal vectors (x,x,x)): 1 for all n >= 1.
%C A400564 - Orbits of size 3 (vectors (x,x,y) with x != y): floor(n/2) + 1 - (1 if 3|n else 0).
%C A400564 - Orbits of size 6 (vectors (x,y,z) with x > y > z >= 0): round(n^2 / 48) if n is even, else 0.
%D A400564 P. A. MacMahon, Combinatory Analysis, Cambridge Univ. Press, London and New York, Vol. 1, 1915 and Vol. 2, 1916.
%H A400564 Jishnu Babu Ranitha, <a href="/A400564/b400564.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A400564 a(n) = 2 + floor(n/2) - (1 if 3|n else 0) + (round(n^2 / 48) if 2|n else 0).
%F A400564 G.f.: 2*x/(1 - x) + x^2 / ((1 - x)*(1 - x^2)) - x^3 / (1 - x^3) + x^6 / ((1 - x^2)*(1 - x^4)*(1 - x^6)).
%e A400564 a(1) = 2: {(1,1,1)} (size 1) and {(1,0,0), (0,1,0), (0,0,1)} (size 3).
%e A400564 a(2) = 3: {(2,2,2)} (size 1), {(1,1,0), (1,0,1), (0,1,1)} (size 3), and {(2,0,0), (0,2,0), (0,0,2)} (size 3).
%e A400564 a(3) = 2: {(3,3,3)} (size 1) and {(3,0,0), (0,3,0), (0,0,3)} (size 3).
%e A400564 a(6) = 5: {(6,6,6)}, {(3,3,0),...}, {(6,0,0),...}, {(4,1,1),...}, and the first size-6 orbit generated by (2,1,0) having coordinate sum 2*(2+1+0) = 6.
%t A400564 Table[2 + Floor[n/2] - Boole[Divisible[n, 3]] + If[EvenQ[n], Round[n^2/48], 0], {n, 1, 50}]
%o A400564 (Python)
%o A400564 def a(n):
%o A400564     return 2 + n // 2 - (1 if n % 3 == 0 else 0) + (round(n**2 / 48) if n % 2 == 0 else 0)
%o A400564 print([a(n) for n in range(1, 51)])
%Y A400564 Cf. A400544 (main partition sequence), A003293, A144677.
%K A400564 nonn,easy,new
%O A400564 1,1
%A A400564 _Jishnu Babu Ranitha_, Sep 30 2026
